        <StdOut>Set apart for WebKit: F-5: WebKit shades a pattern whose tile is a few pixels across darker than Chromium and with a grain, from the one tile the document gives, and otherwise as the pattern's phase falls on the pixels. WebKit's image of marymoor11_lowerlayers has 3 pixels outside the tolerance of Chromium's (each color channel within the range the other image takes within 1 pixel, give or take 4 levels, or at an edge within 40 levels of it, and within 0.4 of the contrast around it, once both are blurred by 1 pixel), by up to 59 levels; see browsers/webkit/differences/marymoor11_lowerlayers.png.</StdOut>
