        <StdOut>Set apart for WebKit: F-5: WebKit draws nothing of a text whose characters are all Runic, in any face and in SVG alone; and WebKit hints the glyphs of the faces the document embeds, as its Linux build does whatever fontconfig, text-rendering or its own settings say, while Chromium draws them unhinted. WebKit's image of fontfallback has 829 pixels outside the tolerance of Chromium's (each color channel within the range the other image takes within 1 pixel, give or take 4 levels, or at an edge within 80 levels of it, and within 0.4 of the contrast around it, once both are blurred by 1 pixel), by up to 251 levels; see browsers/webkit/differences/fontfallback.png.</StdOut>
